{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791698214,"nonce":"01zjSpjwPtxxrO5DDrWyZOWCUwM=","message":"Slice 3 is on main and pushed, ending at c812539a244096bc7e3dc6b3886313715d62bf04. The method reload is bbddaaa5b31524b187f9281392f011f69f399d7f; the fix for compiled frames is 417d8c7220b21ed9fdc3cf6869113f45aaaa582d.\n\nA reload now takes a method added to or removed from a class that is already running. A method keeps the vtable slot it has; a new virtual method, or one that gains a slot because something now overrides it, takes a slot above the class and its subclasses; an override shares its parent's. The new program's prototypes and the calls to them are renumbered onto those slots, the C prototype list and runtime object of each changed class and its subclasses are rebuilt, and every class's vtable is built again after the flush. ashui's tests/fixtures/hotreload v7 (a private helper its render calls) prints the line they specified under the default tiers, --jit-threshold 1, cranelift and llvm; v3 to v6 still reload.\n\nTwo read-only reviews found defects the gates had not, all fixed: a method counted as an override because its slot was below the parent's count (wrong by-name lookups, garbage from toString, writes past the method table), Cranelift's CallMethod loading a vtable that the flush had dropped (a crash in a hot loop over an object made before the reload), a reload whose only change was a removed override being skipped, and a dropped function reading a literal that a new one had taken the slot of (constants are no longer recycled; the spare globals are 65536).\n\nThe NUC found a bug older than the slice. A loop that has been carried into compiled code (main's polling loop, after OSR) called hl.Api.checkReload(), which staged the reload; the interpreter applies a staged reload only when one of its own calls returns, so the calls after checkReload returned true ran the old code, and a loop that is compiled throughout might never apply it. It showed only under load. checkReload now applies the reload before it returns when compiled code calls it. The fixtures poll every millisecond so that main is compiled by reload time, and 15 of the 22 cases failed without the fix.\n\nLeft, none reproduced as a failure: a removed non-virtual method that comes back gets a new findex, so a frame that began before the removal keeps the old body; a zombie method blocks adding the same name to a base class until restart; --mode jit applies a reload now but compiled code keeps the functions it inlined. Next is a field added to a leaf class (ashui's v8), with spare room allocated only under --hot-reload, then statics.","files":null}]}